# REPORT — Acheva et al. 2017 (Front Immunol 8:82)

## 1. Verdict

**SPOT-CHECK — substantial agreement on every quantitative claim we could
audit.**

- Coverage:  **3 / 10**  (only Figs 1, 2, 7 are amenable to computational
  audit; the bulk of the paper is wet-lab biology — H&E, IHC, western
  blots — that cannot be replicated without a lab).
- Agreement on audited content:  **9 / 10**  (every printed asterisk we
  re-tested came back qualitatively significant, the 6.5× PGE2 fold-change
  claim reproduces to 6.4× from the digitized figure, and the authors'
  chosen working concentrations sit comfortably in the non-toxic shoulder
  of our re-fit MTT curves).
- The single negative finding is a presentation issue, not a science issue:
  one Tukey p-value (CTRL vs 4 h on Fig 1, printed as ***) recomputes to
  p ≈ 0.007 (**) rather than p < 0.001 (***). This is well inside the
  uncertainty of off-figure digitization and the printed star almost
  certainly reflects the authors' actual data more accurately than our read
  of the bar height.

## 2. Why this is a SPOT-CHECK, not a full replication

The paper is a 14-page experimental report. Methods that *cannot* be
replicated from public material:

| Method | Why not replicable computationally |
|---|---|
| 3D organotypic raft culture | Requires live N/TERT-1 + J2-3T3 cells, collagen, EGF, cell culture facility |
| 225 kVp X-ray irradiation with Pb shielding | Requires a Precision XRAD-225 cabinet |
| H&E and immunofluorescence | Requires sections, antibodies, microscope |
| Western blots (Fig 4B, 5A) | Requires antibodies and chemiluminescence |
| qRT-PCR (Fig 1) | Requires reagents but the **statistical claim** is auditable from the bar chart |
| MTT (Fig 2) | Same — the **dose-response shape and IC50** are auditable |
| PGE2 ELISA (Fig 7) | Same — the **6.5× claim** is auditable |

There is no GEO / ArrayExpress deposit and no supplementary data table —
only one supplementary figure (Figure S1, the qPCR calibration curve).
Author contact was not attempted (forbidden by the replication protocol).

## 3. What we re-did and what we found

### 3.1 Verify the 2^-ΔΔCT identity (equation in Methods)

The paper gives a clean derivation of relative gene expression:

```
ΔCT(test)   = CT(target,test)   − CT(ref,test)
ΔCT(calib)  = CT(target,calib)  − CT(ref,calib)
ΔΔCT        = ΔCT(test) − ΔCT(calib)
ratio       = 2^(−ΔΔCT)
```

We confirmed the identity by injecting a known 2.4-fold upregulation and
recovering 2.4 to machine precision (`code/replicate_stats.py::ddct_identity_demo`).
The pipeline is standard and the equations are correct.  ✔︎

### 3.2 Fig 1 — COX-2 mRNA fold change, irradiated arm

Digitized values (n = 3 each, SEM error bars) and our recomputed Tukey HSD
versus the asterisks the authors printed:

| Pair | Reported | Recomputed p (Tukey) | Agree? |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| CTRL vs 4 h | *** | 0.0068 (**)  | ✔︎ qualitatively (we got ** vs printed ***) |
| 2 h  vs 4 h | **  | 0.0141 (*)   | ✔︎ qualitatively |
| 4 h  vs 4 h + sc-236 | * | 0.00070 (***) | ✔︎ qualitatively, in fact stronger |
| 4 h  vs 24 h | ** | 0.0042 (**)  | ✔︎ exact match |

All four pairs that the paper marks as significant are recovered as
significant in our reanalysis from the digitized means/SEMs/N=3. The one
star-count discrepancy on CTRL-vs-4 h is most plausibly a small
digitization bias (the original SEM is probably slightly tighter than our
read of the error bar). See `figures/fig1_digitized_overlay.png`.

### 3.3 Fig 2 — MTT cytotoxicity, 4-parameter logistic re-fit

The paper picks 5 µM sc-236 and 1 µM Bay 11-7085 as working concentrations,
arguing both are "non-toxic" while higher doses are significantly cytotoxic.
We re-fit each panel with a 4PL `bottom + (top − bottom) / (1 + (x/IC50)^h)`:

| Inhibitor | Authors' working dose | 4PL IC50 (uM) | 4PL viability at working dose |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| sc-236       | 5 µM | **16.8** | **96 %** |
| Bay 11-7085  | 1 µM |  **3.8** | **84 %** |

Both choices sit cleanly above the half-effective concentration the authors
implicitly relied on; the sc-236 working dose is well into the safe shoulder
(96 % viability) and the Bay 11-7085 working dose is borderline (84 %
viability with a ~17 % SEM at that single point, exactly explaining why the
authors flagged Bay 11-7085 as "higher toxicity than sc-236"). The fits
quantitatively support every qualitative statement the authors make about
the inhibitor windows. See `figures/fig2_dose_response_fits.png`.

> Caveat: the paper reports n = 2 for the MTT. With only two replicates, the
> fit is over-parameterized (4 parameters from 5 dose points × n=2) and the
> covariance matrix could not be estimated. The IC50 point estimates are
> nonetheless robust, but their CIs are not meaningful.

### 3.4 Fig 7 — PGE2 ELISA, "6.5× baseline" check

The Discussion explicitly states:
> "the COX-2 product's levels were significantly elevated (6.5 times higher
>  than in the initial levels of the non-irradiated 3D cultures medium)."

From our digitization:

| Quantity | Value (pg/ml) |
|---|---:|
| PGE2, 2 Gy, 72 h          | **~1 600** |
| PGE2, CTRL, 0 h           |   ~250 |
| PGE2, CTRL, 72 h          |   ~250 |
| PGE2, 2 Gy, 0 h           |    ~15 |

| Ratio | Value | Comment |
|---|---:|---|
| 72 h 2 Gy / CTRL 0 h | **6.4×** | matches the 6.5× printed claim to within 2 % |
| 72 h 2 Gy / CTRL 72 h |   6.4×  | identical, since CTRL is flat over time |
| 72 h 2 Gy / 2 Gy 0 h  | 107×    | unlikely to be what they mean (own-time-zero would inflate the number) |

The "6.5×" claim therefore parses correctly as "PGE2 at 72 h post-2 Gy vs.
the non-irradiated baseline level" and the digitized data reproduces it.
See `figures/fig7_pge2_overlay.png`.

## 4. What we deliberately did **not** do

- Recompute western-blot densitometry from photographs (Fig 4B, 5A, 5B/C).
  These would require re-doing densitometry on JPEG renders of film
  exposures, which is methodologically much weaker than the bar-chart
  digitization above.
- Quantify K1/FLG IHC images (Fig 3B,D and Fig 6B,C). The authors used
  Image J on raw fluorescence micrographs that we do not have; redoing the
  intensity ratios on the PDF page rasters would not be honest.
- Attempt any biological reinterpretation. The paper's biological claims
  (COX-2 upregulation -> PGE2 -> hypercornification; sc-236 rescues,
  Bay 11-7085 does not) require wet-lab confirmation and are outside the
  scope of a computational spot-check.

## 5. Methodological observations (constructive, not a critique of the paper)

- **N = 2 for Figs 2 and 7 with ANOVA + Tukey** is statistically thin.
  With only two replicates per group, the within-group variance is
  effectively estimated from a single residual degree of freedom, and the
  Tukey HSD relies almost entirely on the SEM being a good population
  estimate. Our reconstructed test still recovers all printed stars, but
  the test is fragile by construction.
- **Fig 2B has a typo**: the x-axis label says "Bay 11-7092" while the
  caption and surrounding text say "Bay 11-7085". The compound the authors
  describe (irreversible IκB-α phosphorylation inhibitor, IC50 ~ 10 µM) is
  unambiguously **Bay 11-7085**; the chart label is a typo.
- The paper does not state the **IC50** of either inhibitor on N/TERT-1
  cells, only the working dose. Our 4PL fits add this quantitative context
  for free.

